### Additional comments and feedback

The GUI itself is genuinely easy to use — there are only three controls a
first-time user really needs (paste text, pick a word count, click
**Summarise**), and the streaming output gives clear feedback that something
is happening. The colour palette is consistent and the status bar showing
`Ollama · phi3:mini · Local · Offline` helps reassure the user about what is
going on behind the scenes.

The main usability weakness is **response time**. On a CPU-only laptop, a
75-word summary takes around 56–58 seconds, which is long enough that the
user starts to wonder whether the app has frozen, even with streaming
output. A visible token counter or a progress estimate would help. The lack
of a **Stop button** is the second clear issue — once *Summarise* is
clicked, the only way out is to wait or kill the app.
